{"amendments":[{"body":"Current diff is solving the wrong task. The touched implementation is limited to alkalinity accounting (`crates/tank_core/src/systems/nitrogen_cycle.rs:12`, `crates/tank_core/src/systems/water_change.rs:128`, `crates/tank_core/src/types/process.rs:10`) plus alkalinity-focused tests, but there is still no corresponding change in the shrimp reproduction pipeline/spec data requested by `tanksim-6e5.6.4`. As submitted, none of the required breeding-suppression, egg-dropping, or 2000-hour reproduction scenario acceptance criteria are implemented.","rationale":"This is a task-level correctness gap: the patch does not satisfy the bead it is being reviewed against."},{"body":"`crates/tank_core/src/systems/nitrogen_cycle.rs:346` computes `total_mg_n_nitrified` as `nob_step.oxidized_n_mg + comammox_step.oxidized_n_mg`, while `crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs:232` records that field as the tick's total nitrification. That omits AOB TAN->NO2 oxidation whenever nitrite accumulates, even though that pathway is the one consuming alkalinity/O2. In low-NOB or low-DO scenarios the new trace will therefore report low nitrification while `alk_consumed_meq` shows the opposite.","rationale":"The new debugging/tracing output is supposed to make alkalinity suppression explainable; this metric becomes misleading in exactly the nitrite-bottleneck cases users will inspect."},{"body":"`crates/tank_core/tests/nitrification_alkalinity.rs:1` contains the new regression coverage, but the file is still untracked, so it is absent from `git diff` and would not ship with the patch as reviewed. The submitted change therefore adds runtime behavior without actually delivering the promised test coverage.","rationale":"Without checking in the new test file, the acceptance criteria around alkalinity behavior are not enforced in CI or in the delivered patch."}],"summary":"I reviewed the changed tank-core files end to end and ran targeted tests around cycling, tracing, water-change mass balance, plant normalization, budget tracking, and the new nitrification alkalinity test file. The implementation is mostly coherent, but I found three release-blocking issues: the diff is scoped to alkalinity accounting rather than the requested reproduction task, the new nitrification trace undercounts AOB-only oxidation, and the new alkalinity test file is still untracked so its coverage is not actually part of the patch."}